<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikola Petkov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikola Petkov was a Bulgarian politician, leader of the Bulgarian Agrarian National Union and of the opposition to communist rule after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. A minister in the Fatherland Front government of 1944–45, he broke with the communists and led the opposition in the elections of 1946. He was arrested in 1947, convicted in a show trial and hanged in September 1947, despite protests from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikola-petkov.jpg" alt="Nikola Petkov" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nikola_Petkov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
